  "synonym_discrimination": null,
  "usage_note": "A thing that **cracks** usually has a thin line in it and may still be in one piece; **break** is the general word, used especially when something comes apart. The phrasal verbs **crack down** (deal with something more strictly) and **crack up** (laugh a lot; become mentally ill) are separate entries.",
